{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1859","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1859","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1859\",\"parent_revision\":\"f6ecf4b9cc570daa74bb4a83e12fb61a4357a515\",\"root_revision\":\"b9af5569b9328dae6f6910b37a1f05a54ed3e4a4536fa21ed4d0b6dad2b64102\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add autonomy modes (full_auto/checkpoint/per_task) to implement-feature dispatch loop** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 pattern: Parallel Execution with Configurable Autonomy (feature 3)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-21)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Add `Plan.autonomy` field (`full_auto`/`checkpoint`/`per_task`) to the SAM Plan model and gate the `implement-feature` Progress Loop on the configured mode, so users can choose between uninterrupted execution, wave-level confirmation gates, and per-task confirmation gates.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - `Plan.autonomy: Literal[\\\"full_auto\\\", \\\"checkpoint\\\", \\\"per_task\\\"] = \\\"full_auto\\\"` field confirmed present at `models.py` lines 332\u2013334.\\n  - `_sam_plan_status()` in `server.py` (lines 412\u2013427) calls `backend.read_plan()` and merges `autonomy` key into the returned dict \u2014 same pattern as `_sam_plan_ready`.\\n  - `implement-feature/SKILL.md` Progress Loop (lines 41\u201395, 248\u2013299) branches on `autonomy_mode` for `per_task` serial dispatch, `checkpoint` wave-gate, and `full_auto` (no-gate) paths.\\n  - Commit Ownership section (lines 226\u2013244) correctly gates commit timing on `autonomy_mode`.\\n  - All three test cases (`test_sam_plan_status_includes_autonomy_key`, `test_sam_plan_status_autonomy_defaults_to_full_auto`, `test_plan_model_validate_without_autonomy_defaults_to_full_auto`) confirmed present in `tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` lines 724\u2013826.\\n  - `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` reference `autonomy` field.\\n  - All Q1\u2013Q3 human questions resolved (2026-04-22).\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Test pattern for parametrized three-value validation derived from existing status tests \u2014 confirmed present as `test_plan_model_validate_accepts_all_three_autonomy_values` (lines 804\u2013826).\\n- MISSING: None.\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `sam_plan(action='status')` output contains key `autonomy`.\\n- With `autonomy: per_task` set on the plan and two ready tasks, implement-feature dispatches task 1, reports, and halts for user input before dispatching task 2 (verified by transcript showing the literal prompt string `\\\"Confirm next task\\\"`).\\n- Default behavior for existing plans (no `autonomy` field) matches today's `full_auto` execution \u2014 backward compatible.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe Progress Loop in `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 34\u2013206) dispatches ready tasks in batches without user review between batches. There is no plan-level `autonomy` field on the `Plan` model, and no branch in the SKILL mermaid graph that inserts a user-confirmation gate between waves. The only checkpoint is the Completion Gate after **all** tasks finish \u2014 no intermediate wave-level or task-level gate exists.\\n\\nSymptom: long-running plans are all-or-nothing. A user who wants to review after a foundational wave before letting downstream waves run has no way to ask for that gate short of killing the session.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`Plan.autonomy: Literal[\\\"full_auto\\\", \\\"checkpoint\\\", \\\"per_task\\\"] = \\\"checkpoint\\\"` added to `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py`. `implement-feature/SKILL.md` grows an autonomy-gated branch in its Progress Loop: after each batch (checkpoint) or each task (per_task), the orchestrator reports a compact summary and waits for user confirmation before pulling the next batch. `full_auto` preserves today's behavior. Value readable via `sam_plan(action='status')`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3d040ba2e06e51c8c89e7056b6f71319146992f128bd11b73f34de983a04f026\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnKQwQ\"}"}